{
  "note": "THE PLATFORM ACHIEVEMENTS (the creator, 2026-10-30; docs/achievements.md). One counter progression per group, each achievement on one level of its track. tools/server/make-config.mts writes them into the game config (names and descriptions from locales/<lang>.json, keys achievement.<slug>.name/.desc, the stamps' from achievement.stamped.name/.desc with {{trip}} from names-<lang>.json trip.<id>, each counter's from achievement.count.<counter slug>.name/.desc; the English here only until those keys are written), and fills a missing id once: a counter's from its slug, an achievement's at random. NEVER change an id, a counter's slug or what it counts, an achievement's counter, `at`, `points` or `icon` once it is released: the points budget is lifetime, so a changed achievement is a new one (a new entry, a new id). `counts` is what the win checker (functions/checker/src/count.rs) sets the counter to from the player's progress record, on every verified win: levels, the campaign levels finished (each once); stamps, the trips stamped, in trips.json's order (so stamp k is trip k's); souvenirs, the Souvenirs finished; hard, the hard and super hard campaign levels won; super, the super hard ones; dailies, the dailies won, one a date. `awardsIcon`: it awards an Arcade avatar icon, the game item `icon` (Art's slug, gemctl item upload); until that is set it ships with no reward.",
